  "model_authored_rationale": "Iterated robust tabu search (Taillard Ro-TS) for QAP n=64, sparse heavy-tailed flows.\n\nRationale (unverified hypothesis): the reference runs FAQ plus scipy 2-opt with 16 restarts.\nThat search stops at the first local optimum of each restart. Taillard's robust tabu search\nkeeps O(n^2)-updated swap deltas. It makes about 1e5 moves per second in numba. The search\nis iterated with perturbed restarts from the best solution. It should find solutions well\nbeyond 2-opt local optima within about 20 s per instance. Two nogil threads process\ninstances in parallel.\n\nTime is budgeted per split: at most about 1000 s wall clock and at most 25 s per instance.\nThis leaves margin under the 1800 s prediction and train limits.\n\nLimitations: no tuning was done on development data. The stopping rule is wall clock, so\nresults are not bit-reproducible. Train only compiles the numba code and measures speed.",
