  "review_findings": [
    "The source implements conventional compiled robust tabu search with maintained swap deltas, randomized tenure, aspiration, and perturbations between phases. Both arms use this broad algorithm family; this is not evidence of a newly invented algorithm.",
    "Candidate uses two ThreadPoolExecutor workers and Numba nogil kernels. Per-instance prediction budget is at most 25 seconds, split budget 1000 seconds; each 30000-iteration phase can overrun its individual time check. Actual worker stages, not nominal budgets, determine wall time.",
    "Training compiles and probes only two training instances for about four seconds each. No full-reference comparison is done in training; twelve-second training is not the full 29.314-minute delivery time. The rationale claim of roughly 100000 moves/second is not established by this short probe.",
    "Development/confirmation and final audit independently reproduce host objectives. Final audit improves 8.5573% over the fixed reference and passes the original 2% plus uncertainty gate. Bootstrap is retained, not rerun in this local audit.",
    "Two paid proposals, one unused; all requests for this episode settled. Control is still running, so no prospective QAP paired reduction is asserted."
